{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117104","id":3358736047,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7IMj6v","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117104","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117104.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117104.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117104","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117104/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117104/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117104/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/a7418e39581db82c1577a74c1557896722e1d196","number":117104,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add fixed resolution mode to `SubViewportContainer`.","user":{"login":"EMBYRDEV","id":20043270,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDQzMjcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20043270?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EMBYRDEV","html_url":"https://github.com/EMBYRDEV","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EMBYRDEV/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EMBYRDEV/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EMBYRDEV/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EMBYRDEV/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EMBYRDEV/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EMBYRDEV/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EMBYRDEV/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EMBYRDEV/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EMBYRDEV/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14387\r\n\r\nThis adds a new mode to `SubViewportContainer` that allows the end user to specify a specific resolution rather than the existing behaviour of scaling based on native resolution.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"521\" height=\"364\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4eb28740-77fd-429e-9e71-615b3167e24d\" />\r\n\r\nThis is incredibly useful for developers working on retro games that are designed to emulate specific resolutions and looks.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1165\" height=\"544\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7fed1c2d-91e8-4d09-9466-8ec6c6a3ac57\" />\r\n\r\nFor example if I was making a PSX game I could set the fixed resolution of the `SubViewportContainer` to 320x240.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis needs to be implemented on the engine level as you can somewhat emulate this via implementing your own SVC via script however there is integration within the Viewport class that scales mouse position information and mouse picking (selecting nodes via the mouse) relies on the `SubViewportContainer` class.\r\n\r\nYou can't achieve the same effect by messing with the shrink property since it is an integer, even if it was changed to a float, it feels hacky.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1732720779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzMyNzIwNzc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gui","name":"topic:gui","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","des